From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@arm.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:00:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/meta: correct image-resolve for 3D image

When resolving attachments into 3D images, we need to adjust
dstOffset.z instead of the baseArrayLayer.

This was a latent bug, that happened to work out because PanVK preserved
baseArrayLayer, even if that's actually illegal in Vulkan according to
VUID-VkImageCreateInfo-imageType-00961. This changed in 39a857312aee
("pan/texture: Reuse the layer range as a Z-slice range on 3D views"),
and we started actually misbehaving.

Fixes this VK-CTS test on PanVK:
- dEQP-VK.renderpasses.renderpass1.suballocation.multisample_resolve.resolve_into_3d_image.render_pass_resolve_3_1_1_0

Fixes: 39a857312aee ("pan/texture: Reuse the layer range as a Z-slice range on 3D views")
Fixes: 1a94c556326f ("vulkan/meta: Add support for MSAA resolves")
Reviewed-by: Faith Ekstrand <faith.ekstrand@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2c0adfd4a19d62d98ac255ea88753a35c109eb60)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit a5495156bc8e0094b630beb7648e892f9d2ad738)
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_meta_blit_resolve.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_meta_blit_resolve.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_meta_blit_resolve.c
index 2d74d369e0e..e4ea43abf33 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_meta_blit_resolve.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_meta_blit_resolve.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /*
  * Copyright © 2022 Collabora Ltd
+ * Copyright © 2026 Arm Ltd
  *
  * Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
  * copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"),
@@ -1023,7 +1024,11 @@ vk_meta_resolve_attachment(struct vk_command_buffer *cmd,
       u_foreach_bit(v, view_mask) {
          region.srcSubresource.baseArrayLayer = src_view->base_array_layer + v;
          region.srcSubresource.layerCount = 1;
-         region.dstSubresource.baseArrayLayer = dst_view->base_array_layer + v;
+         uint32_t dst_layer = src_view->base_array_layer + v;
+         if (dst_view->image->image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D)
+            region.dstOffset.z = dst_layer;
+         else
+            region.dstSubresource.baseArrayLayer = dst_layer;
          region.dstSubresource.layerCount = 1;
 
          vk_meta_resolve_image(cmd, meta,
@@ -1034,7 +1039,10 @@ vk_meta_resolve_attachment(struct vk_command_buffer *cmd,
    } else {
       region.srcSubresource.baseArrayLayer = src_view->base_array_layer;
       region.srcSubresource.layerCount = layer_count;
-      region.dstSubresource.baseArrayLayer = dst_view->base_array_layer;
+      if (dst_view->image->image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D)
+         region.dstOffset.z = dst_view->base_array_layer;
+      else
+         region.dstSubresource.baseArrayLayer = dst_view->base_array_layer;
       region.dstSubresource.layerCount = layer_count;
 
       vk_meta_resolve_image(cmd, meta,
-- 
